  "id": "Compound::DB08815 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Lurasidone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Lurasidone may cause Cyp3a4 expression or activity, as it is linked to drug withdrawal syndrome, dyslipidaemia, and cogwheel rigidity, all of which are associated with Prochlorperazine. Prochlorperazine, in turn, binds to Cyp3a4, indicating a potential mechanism by which Lurasidone could influence Cyp3a4 function. The shared lowest common ancestors, such as Piperazines and Agent Affecting Nervous System, further suggest a broader pharmacological context that may underlie these interactions. The evidence points to a possible dependency on Prochlorperazine as a mediator, with Lurasidone potentially modulating Cyp3a4 through this pathway. The integration of these findings supports a mechanism where Lurasidone may influence Cyp3a4 via Prochlorperazine, highlighting a complex interplay between the drug and the enzyme.",
